                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "RPG in the style of RPG Maker, in which you, as Captain Eldon, travel between islands, assemble a crew, and search for the legendary Pirate King's treasure, fighting in turn-based battles\n\n✅The ability to recruit different crew members adds a touch of variety\n✅Good turn-based combat system\n✅Atmospheric pirate adventure with a simple and easy-to-follow treasure hunt motif\n✅Exploration of islands and ship travel\n✅The price is fair\n✅Good soundtrack that fits the game's atmosphere\n\n❌Repetitive combat that becomes routine over time.\n❌Simple plot without major plot twists or character development\n❌The graphics look poor\n❌Limited depth of the combat system and few strategic elements\n\n✅✅ Verdict: [strike] Terrible [/strike] , [strike] Bad [/strike] , [strike] Mediocre [/strike] , [b] Decent [/b] , [strike] Good [/strike] , [strike] Very Good [/strike] (Rating scale for short games, retro indie simulator games and similar)\n\n[quote] If you'd like to see more of my reviews, you can find them on my\ncurator page:\n[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/45994324/admin/reviews_manage/]CuratorKingViking[/url]\nand on my group:\n[url=https://steamcommunity.com/groups/CuratorKingViking]GroupKingViking[/url]\n\nIf you have any questions about my reviews, feel free to ask.\nI’m happy to answer them. All reviews are my own!!\nBest regards, King Viking Bezimienny, Polish Game Reviewer. [/quote]",
